YYYYYummmm...</div></div></div><div class="review media" id="b33d434a-b1dd-4801-ae80-b0a7d5286b74"><a title="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/Shawn3117"><img src="https://x.yummlystatic.com/web/1x1.png"/></a><div class="review-content"><div class="review-name"><a title="Shawn&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="Shawn&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/Shawn3117">Shawn</a> <span class="font-bold greyscale-3 p3-text">3 years ago</span></div><div class="review-rating"><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="1" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="2" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="3" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="4" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="5" data-icon=""></span></div><div class="review-text font-normal p2-text">it was delicious I cooked the garlic cloves in olive oil for about 10 mins on low and then chopped and added to pizza. i also added italian sausage fresh mushrooms and white onions it was amazing.</div></div></div><div class="review media" id="b20de819-3bf4-4a5b-8fe2-04e79b40c6ab"><a title="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/Jb1827"><img src="https://x.yummlystatic.com/web/1x1.png"/></a><div class="review-content"><div class="review-name"><a title="JB&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="JB&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/Jb1827">JB</a> <span class="font-bold greyscale-3 p3-text">3 years ago</span></div><div class="review-rating"><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="1" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="2" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="3" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="4" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon empty-star y-icon" data-star-number="5" data-icon=""></span></div><div class="review-text font-normal p2-text">Added garlic salt and sautéed baby Bella mushrooms. Very tasty.</div></div></div><div class="review media" id="08a9d23a-3716-49dc-ba43-ac4bb8d060b3"><a title="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/Stacey Croley"><img src="https://x.yummlystatic.com/web/1x1.png"/></a><div class="review-content"><div class="review-name"><a title="Stacey Croley&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="Stacey Croley&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/Stacey Croley">Stacey Croley</a> <span class="font-bold greyscale-3 p3-text">3 years ago</span></div><div class="review-rating"><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="1" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="2" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="3" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="4" data-icon=""></span><span class="icon empty-star y-icon" data-star-number="5" data-icon=""></span></div><div class="review-text font-normal p2-text">It was really good. The downsides of it were the garlic tasted raw so I might sauté in a skillet beforehand next time &amp; 14 minutes was too long in our oven so I will probably turn down the heat a little and cook it for a shorter time frame</div></div></div><div class="review media" id="a85b9216-fb58-45cb-913b-01097752f39a"><a title="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="[object Object]&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/FantasticSousChef5043"><img src="https://x.yummlystatic.com/web/1x1.png"/></a><div class="review-content"><div class="review-name"><a title="Mr. Brandon Martin&#x27;s Profile" aria-label="Mr. Brandon Martin&#x27;s Profile" href="/profile/FantasticSousChef5043">Mr. Brandon Martin</a> <span class="font-bold greyscale-3 p3-text">3 years ago</span></div><div class="review-rating"><span class="icon full-star y-icon" data-star-number="1" data-icon="